      },
      "text": "Aviation is a system of extraordinary complexity operating to extraordinarily tight tolerances. A 350-tonne aircraft must depart within minutes of schedule, navigate through 12,000 meters of atmosphere shared with thousands of other aircraft, and land within 30 metres of the centreline. The infrastructure — airports, airspace, ATC systems, and airline operations — makes this routine."
